- **Q: What is distributive behavior and how do you turn it off?** A: When the checked type is a naked generic (not wrapped), TypeScript automatically applies the conditional to each union member separately. To prevent this, wrap the type in a tuple: `[T] extends [U]` instead of `T extends U`.
