## ⚡ Short Answer
CSR (Client-Side Rendering) renders HTML in the browser using JavaScript after downloading a minimal HTML shell, while SSR (Server-Side Rendering) generates the full HTML on the server per request and sends it to the browser ready to display. CSR is great for highly interactive apps where SEO isn't critical, while SSR improves initial load performance and search engine crawlability. Modern frameworks like Next.js blend both approaches to get the best of each.

## 📖 Detailed Explanation
**What it is:** CSR delivers a bare HTML file with a JavaScript bundle; the browser executes the JS to build and display the UI. SSR executes the rendering logic on the server and sends complete HTML to the client on every request.

**Why it exists / problem it solves:** CSR emerged with SPAs (React, Vue, Angular) to enable rich, app-like experiences without full page reloads. SSR solves CSR's two major pain points: slow Time-to-First-Contentful-Paint on low-powered devices/slow networks, and poor SEO because crawlers may not execute JavaScript reliably.

**How it works internally:** In CSR, the server sends `<div id="root"></div>` plus a JS bundle; React (or similar) mounts and renders the component tree entirely in the browser. In SSR, the server runs the same component code in a Node.js environment, serializes it to an HTML string, sends that string to the browser, then the framework "hydrates" the static HTML by attaching event listeners — making it interactive again.

**Benefits:**
CSR: lower server load, fast subsequent navigations, rich interactivity, cheap hosting (static files on CDN).
SSR: faster First Contentful Paint (FCP), better SEO, content visible before JS loads, good for content-heavy or public-facing pages.

**Drawbacks / trade-offs:**
CSR: slow initial load (blank screen until JS parses), poor SEO without extra effort, bundle size grows with app size.
SSR: higher server CPU cost per request, slower Time-to-Interactive (TTI) because hydration still runs, added infrastructure complexity, harder caching.

## 💻 Code Example
```typescript
// ─── NEXT.JS — demonstrating CSR vs SSR side-by-side ───────────────────────

// ✅ SSR: getServerSideProps runs on the SERVER on every request.
// HTML arrives fully populated — great for SEO and first paint.
// pages/products-ssr.tsx
import { GetServerSideProps } from 'next';

interface Props { products: { id: number; name: string }[] }

export default function ProductsSSR({ products }: Props) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {products.map(p => <li key={p.id}>{p.name}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}

export const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async () => {
  // This fetch runs on the server — never exposed to the client
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/products');
  const products = await res.json();
  return { props: { products } };
};


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ✅ CSR: data is fetched in the browser after the component mounts.
// Initial HTML is a loading skeleton — data arrives after JS runs.
// pages/products-csr.tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

export default function ProductsCSR() {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState<{ id: number; name: string }[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Runs ONLY in the browser, after hydration
    fetch('/api/products')
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(data => { setProducts(data); setLoading(false); });
  }, []);

  if (loading) return <p>Loading...</p>; // Crawler sees this — bad for SEO

  return (
    <ul>
      {products.map(p => <li key={p.id}>{p.name}</li>)}
    </ul>
  );
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ✅ HYBRID (ISR / Static + CSR): pre-render at build time, revalidate every
// 60 seconds. Best of all worlds for mostly-static content.
// pages/products-isr.tsx
export const getStaticProps = async () => {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/products');
  const products = await res.json();
  return { props: { products }, revalidate: 60 }; // ISR
};
```

