## ⚡ Short Answer
React Router is a client-side routing library for React that enables navigation between views without full page reloads. It maps URL paths to components and manages browser history using the HTML5 History API. When a route changes, React Router renders the matching component tree while keeping the app shell intact, delivering a true single-page application experience.

## 📖 Detailed Explanation
**What it is:** React Router (v6+) is a declarative, component-based routing library that synchronizes the UI with the URL. It provides components like `<BrowserRouter>`, `<Routes>`, `<Route>`, `<Link>`, `<NavLink>`, and hooks like `useNavigate`, `useParams`, and `useLocation`.

**Why it exists / problem it solves:** Traditional multi-page apps reload the entire page on navigation, destroying React state and causing slow transitions. React Router intercepts link clicks, updates the URL via the History API, and re-renders only the relevant component subtree — giving users instant, stateful navigation.

**How it works internally:** React Router wraps the app in a context provider that holds the current location object. When a `<Link>` is clicked, it calls `history.pushState()` to update the URL without a server request, then triggers a context update. `<Routes>` scans its `<Route>` children, scores each path pattern against the current URL using a ranking algorithm (specificity wins), and renders the best match. The `<Outlet>` component handles nested routes by rendering child route components inside parent layouts.

**Benefits:** Zero full-page reloads, preserved React state across navigation, nested layouts, lazy-loaded routes with `React.lazy`, programmatic navigation, URL params and query string access, and scroll restoration.

**Drawbacks / trade-offs:** Requires server-side fallback configuration (serve `index.html` for all paths) to avoid 404s on hard refresh. SEO needs SSR or pre-rendering (Next.js). Deep nesting can make route definitions harder to trace. Bundle size increases (~50KB for v6).

## 💻 Code Example
